Section 1 (C.R.S. 12-162-107(1)(b)): AN INDIVIDUAL SHALL NOT CARRY A FIREARM OR NONLETHAL WEAPON WHILE PROVIDING OR OFFERING TO PROVIDE PRIVATE SECURITY SERVICES UNLESS THE INDIVIDUAL: (I) IS LICENSED AS A COMMERCIAL SECURITY OFFICER;
Section 1 (C.R.S. 12-162-102(7)): "FIREARM" MEANS A HANDGUN, AS DEFINED IN SECTION 18-12-101 (1)(e.5), OR AS FURTHER DEFINED BY THE BOARD BY RULE.
Section 1 (C.R.S. 12-162-108(2)(d)(II)): TO QUALIFY FOR A FIREARM ENDORSEMENT THAT ALLOWS A LICENSED COMMERCIAL SECURITY OFFICER TO CARRY A FIREARM WHILE PROVIDING COMMERCIAL SECURITY SERVICES, AN APPLICANT MUST PROVIDE PROOF TO THE BOARD THAT THE APPLICANT: (A) HAS COMPLETED AT LEAST SIXTEEN HOURS OF FIREARM SAFETY AND FAMILIARITY TRAINING THAT SATISFIES THE REQUIREMENTS SPECIFIED IN SECTION 12-162-110 (3)(c) AND THAT IS APPROVED BY THE BOARD; AND
